compareMixT -- a number against a string (Tony, 2026-11-06). A string that is a number in full compares by value, with a
warning; any other string has no order against a number, with a warning: every operator false but !=, which is true.
Each pair prints all six operators, and the number-only and string-only pairs are the controls, which must not warn.
Before this ruling a number against a string compared with the string's LENGTH, so 1 vs * read equal. Arithmetic still
reads a string as its length (SEQ 347 R3); only compares changed.
